Y ON 09.12.2019 ASKED BY SHRI AJAY TAMTA, \nHON’BLE M.P. REGARDING VOCATIONAL EDUCATION \n \nSteps taken to provide greater access to employment oriented vocational \neducation throughout the country, including backward regions and border areas \n \nS.No. Programmes offered  No. of \ninstitutions \nNo. of students \nenrolled \nsince inception of \nschemes/programmes \n1. Various skill programmes offered \nby UGC \n188 Community \nColleges(since \n2013-14), 289 \nInstitutions offering \nB.Voc Degree \nProgrammes(since \n2014-15)and 68 \nDDU \nKaushalKendras \n(since 2015-16) \n68,663 \n2. Vocational Degree/Diploma \nPrograms under NSQF for AICTE \napproved Institutions \n473 institutions  \n(since 2018-19) 35,450  \n3. \n \nUnder Skill India Mission, Ministry \nof Skill Development and \nEntrepreneurship is implementing \na flagship scheme \n‘PradhanMantriKaushalVikasYojana \n(PMKVY)’ 2016-20 with an \nobjective to provide skilling to one \ncrore people under Short Term \nTraining (STT) and Recognition of \nPrior Learning (RPL) with an outlay \nof 12,000 crore. \nCentrally Sponsored \nCentrally Managed \n(CSCM) being \nimplemented by \nNational Skill \nDevelopment \nCorporation (NSDC)  \n(Since 2016-20) \n \n33,88,235 student (under \nCSCM –STT), 1,68,267 \nstudents (under CSCM-\nSpecial Project) and \n32,10,783 students \n(under CSCM-RPL) \nCentrally Sponsored \nState Managed \n(CSSM) being \nimplemented by \nState Skill \nDevelopment \nMissions (SSDMs) of \nthe States / UTs \npopularly known as \nState- Engagement \nComponent of \nPMKVY \n5,86,787  \nTotal 74,58,185 \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_300": "LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 300 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 9th DECEMBER 2019 \n \n Investment in Oil Exploration \n*300.   SHRIMATI MEENAKSHI LEKHI: \nपेट्रोलियम और प्राक ृ लिक गैस मंत्री \n          Will the Minister of PETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the steps taken to increase the investment in oil exploration and refining in the \ncountry; \n(b)   the steps taken to check the quantity of petcoke produced from crude oil; and \n(c)   the details of the measures taken for the disposal of emission of petcoke i n the \nenvironment considering the health and environmental threat it poses? \n \nANSWER \nपेट्रोलियम और प्राक ृ लिक गैस मंत्रािय में मंत्री (प्रााप्र ामेर्मध ीी)  \nMINISTER IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS \n \n                                       (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n(a) to (c)  A statement is laid on the table of the house. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (C) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO 300 “INVESTMENT IN OIL EXPLORATION” \n(a)  The major initiatives taken by the Government to increase investment in oil \nexploration and refining in the country include:- \n i. Implementation of Hydrocarbon Exploration Licensing Policy                  \n  (HELP) and Open Acreage Licensing Policy (OALP). \n           ii. Dissemination of Geo -scientific d ata through National data                        \n  repository (NDR). \n iii. Early Monetization of Discovered Fields including small &                    \n  Marginal fields. \n iv. Extension of Existing Production Sharing Contracts (PSCs). \n v. Appraisal of unap prised Areas in various sedimentary basins              \n  under National Seismic Program and Multi -client Geo -scientific                   \n  Surveys/ activities in order to enable systematic exploration in                     \n  these areas. \n vi. Re-Assessment of Hydrocarbon Resources in the Country. \n vii. Indian refineries have planned capacity addition through both                    \n  Greenfield and brownfield projects.  \n The Government in February, 2019 approved major reforms in exploration \nand licensing policy to enhance exploration activities, attract domestic and foreign \ninvestment and accelerate domestic production of oil and gas from existing fields. \nThe policy reforms inter-alia aims to boost exploration activities with greater \nweightage to work prog ramme, simplified fiscal and contractual terms, bidding of \nexploration blocks under Category II and III sedimentary basins without any \nproduction or revenue sharing to Government, early monetization of discoveries by \nextending fiscal incentives, incentiviz ing gas production including marketing and \npricing freedom, induction of latest technology and capital, more functional freedom \nto National Oil Companies for collaboration and private sector participation for \nproduction enhancement methods in nomination fi elds, streamlining approval \nprocesses and promoting ease of doing business including electronic single window \nmechanism. \n(b)   New technologies like Petcoke Gasification and circulating fluidised bed boilers \nare adopted for minimising Petcoke generations from refineries. \n(c)  Use of Petcoke has been banned in Uttar Pradesh, Haryana, Rajasthan and \nDelhi. Import duty on Petcoke has also been increased from 2.5% to 10%. Use of \nPetcoke is permitted only in selected industries like cement, lime, calcium carbide,  \naluminium/calciners and gasifiers on user basis.  \n********** ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_301": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 301 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 10.12.2019 \n \nPRADHAN MANTRI GRAM SADAK YOJANA \n \n301. SHRI HEMANT TUKARAM GODSE:  \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether all villages in the State of Maharashtr a have been connected through all weather \nroads under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (P MGSY) and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(b) the number of villages which are yet to be conn ected under the said Yojana in the above \nState; and \n(c) the time by which such villages are likely to b e connected? \n        \n       ANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n                                            (SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n(a) to (c):  A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 301 \ndue for answer on 10.12.2019 \n(a) to (c):  Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) is a one- time special intervention \nto provide rural connectivity, by way of a single a ll-weather road, to the eligible unconnected \nhabitations in the core network with a population o f 500 persons and above in plain areas and \n250 persons and above in Hills, North East, Tribal and Desert Areas as per Census 2001. In the \ncritical Left Wing Extremism (LWE) affected blocks (as identified by Ministry of Home \nAffairs), additional relaxation has been given to c onnect habitations with a population of 100 \npersons and above. The unit of programme under PMGS Y is a habitation and not a revenue \nvillage.  \n \nAgainst total eligible habitations of 1950 (in the category of 500+ population in plain areas and \n250+ population in tribal areas) for coverage under  PMGSY in the State of Maharashtra, 1803 \nhabitations have already been provided all weather road connectivity including 480 habitations \nprovided connectivity under State scheme. Out of ba lance habitations, 122 habitations have \neither been dropped or not feasible. Remaining 25 h abitations are targeted to be connected by all \nweather roads at the earliest. \n \nUnder 100-249 population size in LWE areas, against  188 eligible habitations, 90 habitations \nhave already been provided road connectivity includ ing 67 habitations under State scheme. Out \nof balance 98 habitations, 31 habitations are repor tedly not feasible. The State Government has \ninformed that the remaining 67 habitations are targeted to be connected at the earliest.  \n \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_302": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n302\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n  \n10\nTH\n \nDECEMBER, 2019\n \n \n \nCOMPENSATION UNDER PMFBY\n \n \n*302. \n    \nDR. SUBHAS SARKAR: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has paid compensation under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal \nBima Yojana \n \n(PMFBY) for farmers’ loss in crop \nproduction in the State of West Bengal; \nand\n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof during the last three years, district\n-\nwise?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) &\n \n(\nb\n):\n \nA \nstatement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO \nIN REPLY TO PARTS (a) &\n \n(\nb\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.\n  \n302\n   \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n10\nTH\n  \nDECEMBER, 2019\n.\n \n(a) & (b):\n \nAs per provisions of Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana \n(\nPMFBY\n)\n,\n \nintroduced in \nthe country from Kharif 2016 season, \nclaims for wide spread calamities like flood, drought \netc. or season end claims are worked out and settled by the concerned insurance company \non area approach basis, on receipt of yield data arrived throu\ngh requisite number of  Crop \nCutting Experiments (CCEs) at the end of the harvesting period, from the concerned State \nGovernment.  \n \nHowever, losses due to localized risks of hailstorm, landslide, inundation, cloud burst \n& natural fire and post\n-\nharvest loss\nes are calculated on individual insured farm level, based \non the report of the joint committee comprising of representatives of the State Government \nand the concerned insurance company to survey the extent of loss.  Further, there  is also a \nprovision to p\nay claims towards prevented sowing/failed germination and adhoc claims in \ncase of mid season adversity.  \n \n \nWest Bengal State opted for the scheme in Kharif 2016 season and implemented the \nPMFBY and Restructured Weather Based Crop Insurance Scheme (RWBCIS) \ntill Rabi 2018\n-\n19.  The State Government of West Bengal is implementing its own crop insurance scheme \nfrom Kharif 2019 season.  Details of claims paid in West Bengal under PMFBY and RWBCIS \nare given below :\n \n                                                 \n                                                                  \n(Rs. in crore)\n \nSeason\n \nAdmissible Claim Amount\n \nApproved Claim Amount\n \nClaims Amount paid\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n421.70\n \n421.70\n \n418.24*\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n257.11\n \n256.63\n \n256.63\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n372.23\n \n189.44\n \n173.89**\n \n*   \nClaims are pending due to National Electronic Fund Transfer (NEFT) failure.\n \n** Claims are pending due to non\n-\nreceipt of State Government share in premium subsidy. \n \n \n            \nDistrict\n-\nwise details of claims under PMFBY for last three years in West Bengal are \nannexed\n.\n \n\nAnnexure\n \n \nDetails of claims under PMFBY and RWBCIS in West Bengal  during 2016\n-\n17\n \nDistrict Name\n \nKharif 2016\n \nRabi 2016\n-\n17\n \nYear 2016\n-\n17\n \nEstimated \nClaims \nAmount\n \nApproved \nClaims \nAmount\n \nPaid \nClaims \nAmount\n \nEstimated \nClaims \nAmount\n \nApproved \nClaims \nAmount\n \nPaid \nClaims \nAmount\n \nEstimated \nClaims \nAmount\n \nApproved \nClaims \nAmount \n \nPaid Claims \nAmount\n \n(Rs. in Lakhs)\n \nAlipurduar\n \n120.86\n \n120.86\n \n84.92\n \n0.00\n \n0.00\n \n0.00\n \n120.86\n \n120.86\n \n84.92\n \nBankura\n \n209.10\n \n209.10\n \n202.51\n \n1292.95\n \n1292.95\n \n1292.95\n \n1502.05\n \n1502.05\n \n1495.46\n \nBirbhum\n