    "ls|LS17_S2_U_388": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 388\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 19TH NOVEMBER, 2019/ KARTIKA 28, 1941 (SAKA)\nCYBER CRIME\n388.     SHRI UNMESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL:\nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government is aware that the younger generation are more\nvulnerable to cyber crimes;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the Government has any plan to include cyber crime awareness\nas part of curriculum of the students apart from making stringent laws to\ncontrol the crime; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY)\n(a) & (b): With the increase in use of cyber space, vulnerability of younger\ngeneration to cyber crimes has also increased.\n(c) to (d): National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\nhas developed and shared one brochure\n(http://ciet.nic.in/upload/Cyber%20safety.pdf) and three guidelines booklets\n(http://ciet.nic.in/pages.php?id=booklet-on-cyber-safety&In=en&In=en) on\ncyber safety and security for teachers, students and schools with the States/\nUTs. Details are as below:\n\n-2-\nL.S.US.Q.NO.388 FOR 19.11.2019\n (i) Booklet for Schools covers –Identifying threats vulnerability and assess\nrisk exposure; Develop protection and detection measures; Protect sensitive\ndata; Respond to and recover from cyber security incidents; Educate\nconcerned stakeholders, etc.\n(ii) Booklet for Teachers covers – Social aspects, ethical aspects, legal\naspects, technical aspects; Do’s and Don’ts, etc.\n(iii) Booklet for Students covers – Handling devices, social media, Mailing and\nbrowsing, information seeking and sharing, cyber behavior: Do’s and Don’ts,\netc.\nThe Ministry of Home Affairs has also published a handbook for\nAdolescents/Students on Cyber Safety, in order to make them aware about\nvarious types of cyber crimes and how to protect themselves from such\ncrimes. The handbook has been sent to all State Governments/ Union\nTerritories for wide circulation.  The soft copy of handbook is available on\nwww.mha.gov.in and www.cybercrime.gov.in. This handbook is also shared\non NCERT website by MHRD.\n********",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_389": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. †389 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19TH NOVEMBER, 2019  \nSchemes of Fisheries \n \n†389. DR. RAM SHANKAR KATHERIA:   \n             SHRI RAVI KISHAN:       \n  \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING मत्स्यपालन, \nपशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n (a)    whether the Government has framed any scheme in the interest of farmers engaged in fisheries;  \n(b)     if so, the number of people benefited through such schemes and the details thereof, State-wise;  \n(c)    whether any scheme is likely to be prepared by the Government in the coming years, through \nwhich small fishing farmers can be connected with fisheries; and  \n(d)    if so, the time by which such schemes will be finalized and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \n(SHRI PRATAP CHANDRA SARANGI) \n(a) and  (b)  :   Yes, Sir.  The Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and \nDairying since the financial year 2015 -16 has been implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) \non Blue Revolution: Integrated Development and Management of Fisheries at a total central outlay of \nRs.3000 crore for development of fisheries in the country especially with farmer eccentric activities. The \nCSS aims (i ) to increase the overall fish production in a responsible and sustainable manner for \neconomic prosperity, (ii) to moder nize the fisheries sector with special focus on new technologies , (iii) \nto ensure food and nutritional security  in the country, (iv ) to generate employment and export earnings  \nand (v) to ensure inclusive development and empower fishers and aquaculture farmers.   \n In order to address the infrastructural requirements for fisheries sector, the Department of \nFisheries during 2018-19 has created a dedicated fund namely Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure \nFund (FIDF) a fund size of Rs 7522.48 crore. Under th e FIDF, concessional finance is provided for \ndevelopment fisheries infrastructure in the country . Besides, the Kisan Credit Card (KCC) facility has \nbeen extended to fishers and fish farmers to help them to meet their working capital needs.  \n As per the statistical information compiled in the Department of Fisheries, the fisheries sector \nprovides livelihood to 16.00 million fishers population at the primary level to inland fishers, marine \nfishers, fish farmers and almost twice the number along the value chain. The activities covered under \nabove said are directly or indirectly benefiting these fishers and fish farmers.  \n(c) and (d)  : In addition to the above mentioned ongoing schemes , the Government of India in its \nBudget, 2019 announced a focus ed scheme Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana ( PMMSY) \naiming to establish a robust fisheries management framework and to address the critical gaps in the \nvalue chain, including infrastructure, modernisation, traceability, production, productivity, post \nharvest management and quality control. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_390": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 390 \nANSWERED ON 19.11.2019 \n \nELECTRIC BUSES \n \n390. SHRI P.V. MIDHUN REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES  भारी उद्योग \nएवं ऱोक उद्यम मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has approved/sanctioned 5595 electric buses to 64 Cities/State \nGovt. Entities/STUs  recently for intra -city and inter -city operation under phase -II of the \nFAME India Scheme; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the  number of buses allotted to the State of  Andhra \nPradesh in the current financial year? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n******** \n(a) & (b): Yes, Sir, the Government has sanctioned 5095 electric buses to 64 Cities / State \nTransport Corporations for intra -city operation; 400 electric buses for intercity operation \nand 100 electric buses for last mile connectivity to Delhi Metro Rail Corporation (D MRC) \nunder Phase-II of FAME India Scheme. The number of e -buses allotted to different cities \nof the State of Andhra Pradesh are as given below: - \n \nS.No. Name of City E-Bus allocated \n1. Visakhapatnam 100 \n2. Vijayawada 50 \n3. Amravati 50 \n4. Tirupati 50 \n5. Kakinada 50 \n6. Andhra Pradesh State Road Transport Corporation - \nInter-City Operations \n50 \nTotal 350 \n   \n The expenditure of Rs. 175 crore (approx.) for purchase of these buses is being \nborn by the Department of Heavy Industry. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_391": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 391 \nANSWERED ON 19.11.2019 \n \nJAGI ROAD AND PANCHGRAM PAPER MILLS \n \n391. SHRI PRADYUT BORDOLOI: \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES भारी उद्योग \nएवं ऱोक उद्यम मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that the employees of Jagiroad and Panchgram Paper \nMills of the HPCL have  not been receiving their salaries and dues  for the last 35 months \nand that several of the highly distressed employees have committed suicides; \n  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the action plan proposed to be  taken by the Ministry to salvage and  operationalize the \nJagiroad and Panchgram  Paper Mills of HPCL and payment of dues  and salaries to the \nemployees of these mills? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n******** \n \n(a) to (c) Cachar Paper Mill, Panchgram and Nagaon Paper Mill, Jagiroad  are mills of \nHindustan Paper Corporation Limited (HPC) in Assam. These mills are not in operation. \nThe National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) through an order dated 13.06.2018 \ndirected initiation of Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process under the Insolven cy and \nBankruptcy Code (IBC), 2016 against HPC.  Thereafter, as per the provisions of IBC, the \nBoard of Directors of HPC stood suspended and a Resolution Professional (RP) and a \nCommittee of Creditors were appointed for HPC. \n  \n       The Chairman and Managi ng Director, HPC had filed an appeal in the National \nCompany Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT) against the aforementioned NCLT order \ndated 13.06.2018. The said appeal was dismissed by the Appellate Tribunal vide order \ndated 08.01.2019. \n  \n       The NCLT, during the hearing of the case on 02.05.2019,  ordered for the liquidation \nof HPC and appointed an Official Liquidator for HPC. Subsequently, NCLAT on \n29.05.2019 directed the Official Liquidator, HPC to ensure that the HPC remains a  'going \nconcern' during the liquidation.   The Official Liquidator, HPC  is proceeding as per the \nprovisions of the Indian Bankruptcy Code 2016. \n \n**********  ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_392": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.392  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.11.2019 \n \nFUNDS TO MGNREGS \n \n392. SHRI PARTHIBAN S.R.: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of works taken up in Salem district in Tamil Nadu during the last three years \nunder the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme \n(MGNREGS); \n(b) the quantum of funds sanctioned and utilised during  the said period along with the \ncriteria adopted to take up the works, year-wise; and \n(c) the details of workforce engaged under MGNREGS alon g with the wages paid to them \nduring the said period, gender-wise? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a)&b):   As per the information shared by State Government  of Tamil Nadu, the details of \nworks taken up and the quantum of funds sanctioned and utilized in Salem District in Tamil \nNadu during the last three years is given below:  \n  \nFinancial Year 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 \nNumbe r of works taken up  14704  13675  27577  \nFunds sanctioned  \n(Rs. in lakh) \n27900  25383  28654  \nFunds utilised (Rs. in lakh)  34264  24311  24037  \n \nMahatma Gandhi NREGA is a demand driven wage employ ment programme having bottom \nup approach and priorities of work are set at Gram Sabha level. \n \n(c):  As per the information shared by State Government of Tamil Nadu, the details of  \ngender-wise workforce engaged under Mahatma Gandhi NREGS alongwith the wages paid to \nthem during the last three years are given below: \n  \nYear Workforce engaged Wages paid  \n(Rs. in lakh) Men  Women  \n2016 -17  10893  268418  16068.18  \n2017-18 12300 250583 17188.93  \n2018-19 11617 217634 17317.15  \nTotal 34812 736638 50578.26  \n\n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_393": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & puBt-tc DtsTRtBUTtON\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AI{D PUBLIC DISTRTBUTION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTIOil NO. 393\nTO BE ANSWERED ON lgth NOVEMBER,2O{9\nNATIONAL FOOD SECURITY MISSTON\n393. SHRI HIBI EDEN:\nWall the Minister of GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND pUBLtc\nDISTRIBUTION Jq!tr{f,r xrra, sr{c gt{ grffif,fi Ef{ur d+ be pteased to\nstate:\n(a) the details of the current status of supplementary food progtammes\nin lndia;\n(b) the current status of the National Food Security Missionl\n(c) whether the Government has any plan to provide any special\npackages for the reassessment of various nutrition schemes which are\nnot working properl$ and\n(d) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF GONSUMER AFFA|RS, FOOD &\nPUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\n(sHRl DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO)\n(a): Government enacted that National Food Security Act, 2O{3 (NFSA) in\nJuly 2O{3 with an intended coverage of upto 75o/o ol rural population and\nupto 50% of urban population for receiving highly subsidized foodgrains\nunder Targeted Public Distribution System. One of the guiding principles of\nthe Act is its life cycle approach wherein special provisions for\nsupplementary nutrition have been made for pregnant women and\nlactating mothers and children in the age group of 6 months to 14 yearc.\nEvery pregnant woman and lactating mother is entitled to meal,\nfree of charge, during pregnancy and six months after the child\nbirthn through the local anganwadi, so as to meet the specified\nnutritional standards and also matemity benefit of not less than\nrupees six thousand to partly compensate for the wage loss\nduring the period of pregnancy and also to supplement nutration.\nt.\n\n.\nlv.\nEvery child in the age group of six months to six years, is\nentitled to age appropriate meal, free of charge, through the\n!oca! anganwadi so as to meet the specified nutritional\nstandards\nIn the case of children, up to class Vlll or within the age group\nof six to fourteen years, whichever is applicable, one mid-day\nmeal, free of charge is provided every day except on schoot\nholidays, in al! schools run by !oca! bodies, Government and\nGovernment aided schools, so as to meet the specilied\nnutritional standards.\nState Government through the local anganwadi, also identify\nand provide meals, free of charge, to children who suffer from\nmalnutrition, so as to meet the specified nutritional standalds.\n(b): National Food Security Missaon (NFSM) was launched in 2OO7.08 to\nincrease the production of rice, wheat and pulses through (i) area\nexpansion and productivity enhancement, (ii) restoring soil fertility and\nproductivity, (iii) Greating employment opportunities and (iv) enhancing\nfarm level economy. Goarse cereals were also included in the Mission from\n201+15 under ]IFSM. The interventions covered under NFSM include\ncluster demonstrations on improved package of practices, demonstrations\non cropping system, Seed distribution of high yielding varieties, farm\nmachineries/resources conservation machineries/tools, efficient water\napplication tools, plant protection measures, nutrient managemenUsoi!\nameliorants, cropping system based trainings to the farmers etc. NFSM\ncontinued during {2h Five Year Ptan with the target of additional\nproduction of 25 million tonnes of food grains. Beyond the {2s Plan, the\nmission is being continued with new additional target of 13 million tonnes\nof foodgrains from 2017-18 to 2O19-2O. The country achieved bumper\nproduction of foodgrains during 2O174A at 285.O{ million tonnes. As per 46\nAdvance Estimates total foodgrains production achieved durlng 2O{8-{9 is\n2E4.95 million tonnes. NFSM is being implemented in identified districts of\n29 states in the country.\n(c) & (d): The supplementary nutrition programmes envisaged under the\nItationa! Food Security Act for pregnant women and lactating motherc and\nchildren upto the age of {4 years are operating smoothly and no proposal\nto reassess these programmes is under consideration of the Government.",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_394": "भारत सरकार \nभारी उद्योग और लोक उद्यम मंत्रालय \nलोक उद्यम विभाग \n \nलोक सभा \nअतारांककत प्रश्न संख् या 394   \n \nकदनांक 19 निम् बर, 2019 को उत् तर देने क े  वलए \n \nसीपीएसई का काययकरण  \n394. श्री धैययशील संभाजीराि माणे: \n  \n क् या भारी उद्योग और लोक उद्यम मंत्री यह बताने की क ृ पा करेंगे कक : \n   \n(क) ितयमान में सरकार क े  विवभन् न मंत्रालय/वविभाग/ क े  अंतगयत महारा्‍ र सवहत देश में काययरत क े न् रीय \nसरकारी क्षेत्रक उद्यम (सीपीएसई) की संख् या ककतनी है; \n)ख(  राज् यवसंघ राज् यक्षेत्र-िार विशेषकर महारा्‍ र में ेसक े  अंतगयत क क ल ककतना वनिेश ककया गया है;   \n(ग) विगत तीन िषों क े  प्रत् येक िषय और ितयमान िषय क े  दारान सीपीएसई वारारा ई ई क क ल हावन का ‍ यारा \nक् या है; और  \n(घ)  सरकार वारारा घाटे में चल रही सीपीएसई क े  पकनरूद्धार हेतक ककए गए प्रयास/ का ‍ यारा क् या है? \n \nउत्तर \nभारी उद्योग और लोक उद्यम मंत्री \n(श्री प्रकाश जािडेकर) \n \n(क):  संसद में कदनांक 27.12.2018 को प्रस् तकत ककए गए लोक उद्यम सि्ष ाण 2017-18 क े  अनकसार, कदनांक \n31.03.2018 को विवभन् न मंत्रालय/वविभाग/ क े  अंतगयत महारा्‍ र सवहत देश में 339 सीपीएसईज काययरत थे।   \n(ख):  कदनांक 31.03.2018 की वस्थवत क े  अनकसार पंजीक ृ त कायायलय क े  स् थान क े  ाधार पर सीपीएसईज में \nककए गए रा ज् यवक े न् र शावसत प्रदेश  वनिेश (शेयर प ंजी प् लस दीघयकालीन उधार  रावशयां) का ‍ यारा अनकबंध में \nकदया गया है।  \n(ग):  गत तीन िषय क े  दारान सीपीएसईज को ई ई हावनय/ का ‍ यारा वनम् नवलवखत है:-  \nिषय घाटे में चल रहे सीपीएसईज की संख् या घाटे में चल रहे सीपीएसईज को हावन  \n(रूपए करोड में) \n2015-16 79 -30756 \n2016-17 81 -27480 \n2017-18 71 -31261 \n \n(घ): लोक उद्यम विभाग ने ''रूग् णवशकरूाती रूग् ण तथा कमजोर सीपीएसईज क े  पकनरूद्धार एिं पकनगयठन क े  वलए \nतंत्र को यकविसंगत बनाना'' पर कदनांक 29.10.2015 को कदशावनद्श जारी ककए। ेन कदशावनद्श/ क े  अनकसार, \nसीपीएसईज क े  काययवन्‍ पादन की वनगरानी करने का उत् त रदावयत् ि संबंवधत प्रशासवनक मंत्रालयवविभाग का \nहोता है और सीपीएसईज क े  वलए पकनरूद्धारवपकनगयठनवविवनिेशवबंद करने संबंधी योजनाओं का प्रवतपादन करते \nई ए  वनिारण संबंधी उपाय करते हैं और सक्षम प्रावधकारी क े  अनकमोदन की प्रावि क े  पश् चात योजनाओं को \nकायायवन्ित करते हैं।   \n \n\nअनकबंध \nसीपीएसई का काययकरण  क े  संबंध में प छे गए कदनांक 19.11.2019 क े लोक सभा अतारांककत प्रश्न संख् या 394 क े  \nउत्तर क े भाग (ख) में संदर्भभत अनकबंध \n \nकदनांक 31.03.2018 की वस्थवत क े  अनकसार पंजीक ृ त कायायलय क े  स् थान क े  ाधार पर सीपीएसईज में ककए गए \nराज् यवक े न् र शावसत प्रदेश वनिेश (शेयर प ंजी प् लस दीघयकालीन उधार रावशयां) का ‍ यारा। \nक्रम सं. राज् यवक े न् र शावसत प्रदेश वनिेश (शेयर प ंजी प् लस दीघयकालीन उधार रावशयां)  \n(रूपए करोड में)  \n1 अंडमान और वनकोबार ववारपसम ह 319 \n2 ांध्र प्रदेश  11,570 \n3 अरूणाचल प्रदेश  1 \n4 असम 14,280 \n5 वबहार  733 \n6 चंडीगढ़  264 \n7 छत् तीसगढ़  2,645 \n8 कदल् ली  1,133,055 \n9 गोिा  78 \n10 गकजरात  16 \n11 हररयाणा  32,725 \n12 वहमाचल प्रदेश  6,402 \n13 जम् मक और कश् मीर  111 \n14 झारखंड  8,074 \n15 कनायटक  13,013 \n16 क े रल  3,798 \n17 मध् य प्रदेश  3,247 \n18 महारा्‍ र  76,850 \n19 मवणपकर  118 \n20 मेघालय  9,878 \n21 नागालैण् ड  185 \n22 ओवडशा  1,869 \n23 पांवडचेरी 2 \n24 पंजाब  969 \n25 राजस् थान  524 \n26 तवमलनाडक  22,463 \n27 तेलंगाना  913 \n28 उत् तर प्रदेश  1,424 \n29 उत् तरांचल  6,098 \n30 पविम बंगाल  21,790 \n क क ल 1,373,412 \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_396": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 396 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 19th NOVEMBER, 2019 \n \nSuvidha Programme  \n \n396. SHRIMATI KIRRON KHER:  \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS¸ be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the salient features of Suvidha programme started under the Pradhan Mantri \nBhartiya Janaushadhi Pariyojana (PMBJP);  \n \n(b) the number of stores where Suvidha sanitary napkins are available, State -wise \nincluding Chandigarh; and  \n \n(c) the steps taken by the Government to publicize the programme through Television, \nRadio, Print and other forms of media? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER IN THE MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \n(SHRI D. V. SADANANDA GOWDA)                                \n   \n(a)   Sale of  ‘Janaushadhi Suvidha’ Oxo -Biodegradable Sanitary pad was launched \nunder PMBJP on 4 th June, 2018. Initially these sanitary pads were made available for \nsale at Rs. 2.50/- per pad.   \n \nIn order to make these sanitary pads more affordable, Government of India decided to \nmake these pads available at the rate of only Rs 1.00/ - per pad. From 27.08.2019, \nthese pads are available @ Rs 1.00/- per pad at all Janaushadhi Kendras.  \n(b) ‘Janaushadhi Suvidha’ Sanitary pads are available in all PMBJP Stores. State -wise \nnumber of stores, including Chandigarh, where Suvidha sanitary pads are available, is \nenclosed as Annexure-I. \n \n(c) The awareness about this programme is being spread through advertisements in \nPrint Media, Radio advertisements, TV advertisements , Cinema  advertisements, \nOutdoor publicity is done through Hoardings, Bus Queue Shelters, Bus branding, Auto \nwrapping. In addition to this, social media platforms like facebook, twitter, are be ing \nutilized. Awareness workshops are also conducted. \n\nAnnexure-I \n                    \nThe statement referred to in  part (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Q. No. 396 for 19.11.2019 \nraised by SHRIMATI KIRRON KHER regarding Suvidha Programme \n \nState wise list of PMBJP Kendras where Suvidha sanitary pads are available as on \n11.11.2019 \nSl. No. Name of the State/UT No. of PMBJP Kendras  \n1 Andaman & Nicobar 2 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 185 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 24 \n4 Assam 81 \n5 Bihar 153 \n6 Chandigarh 5 \n7 Chhattisgarh 209 \n8 Dadar & Nagar Haveli 14 \n9 Daman & Diu 4 \n10 Delhi 119 \n11 Goa 8 \n12 Gujarat 507 \n13 Haryana 168 \n14 Himachal Pradesh 59 \n15 Jammu and Kashmir 77 \n16 Jharkhand 55 \n17 Karnataka 567 \n18 Kerala 487 \n19 Ladakh 2 \n20 Lakshadweep 0 \n21 Madhya Pradesh 154 \n22 Maharashtra 395 \n23 Manipur 35 \n24 Meghalaya 1 \n25 Mizoram 21 \n26 Nagaland 16 \n27 Odisha                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             188 \n28 Puducherry 15 \n\n29 Punjab 180 \n30 Rajasthan 132 \n31 Sikkim 2 \n32 Tamil Nadu 570 \n33 Telangana 118 \n34 Tripura 24 \n35 Uttar Pradesh 879 \n36 Uttarakhand 182 \n37 West Bengal 116 \n Total  5754 \n* Medicines are directly supplied to Union Territory of Lakshadweep  \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_397": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 397 \nANSWERED ON 19.11.2019 \n \nSETTING UP OF INDUSTRY FOR EDUCATED YOUTH \n \n397. SHRI OMPRAKASH BHUPALSINH ALIAS PAWAN \nRAJENIMBALKAR: \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES  भारी उद्योग \nएवं ऱोक उद्यम मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of the Central schemes  to provide employment to the growing  number of \nwell-educated youth in the country; \n \n(b) the action taken by the  Government on the request of local MP  who had demanded to \nbuild/create an industry like Bharat Heavy Electricals Ltd. on the available 373 hectares of \nland under  Osmanabad Maharashtra Industrial  Development Corporation (MIDC) to  \nprovide employment to this section of  unemployed youth during zero hour on  21 June \n2019; and \n \n(c) the steps being taken by the  Government to stop the migration of well  educated \nunemployed youth from  Osmanabad district to other districts due  to unseasonal rains, \ndrought hit farming, under developed MIDC and absence of employment opportunities? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n******** \n \n(a):   All PSUs and units of Heavy Industry recruit youths as per requirement. \n \n(b):   Setting up of industries is a state subject. \n \n(c):   Does not pertain to the Department of Heavy Industry. \n***********  ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_398": "O.I.H \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 398 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19TH NOVEMBER, 2019 \n \nPROMOTION OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n \n 398. SHRI UDAY PRATAP SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING मत्स्यपालन, पशुपालन और डेयरी \nमंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the details of the steps taken by the Government to promote animal husbandry and dairying along with \nencouraging the farmers during the last three years and the current year \n  \n(b) the amount of funds allocated and utilized for animal husbandry and dairying in Madhya Pradesh during \nthe abovementioned period; and \n \n(c) the details of income and employment cr eated in animal husbandry and dairying industry in the country \nespecially in Madhya Pradesh during the said period, State-wise?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n(a) The Government is implementing various schemes to complement and supplement the efforts of \nStates/UTs for promotion of animal husbandry  and dairying along with encouraging the farmers during the \nlast three years and the current year such as; \n \ni. Rashtriya Gokul Mission (RGM) \nii. National Programme for Dairy Development (NPDD) \niii. National Dairy Plan-I (NDP-I) \niv. Dairy Entrepreneurship Development Scheme (DEDS) \nv. Dairy Processing and Infrastructure Development Fund (DPIDF) \nvi. Supporting Dairy Cooperatives and Farmer Producer Organizations engaged in dairy activities \n(SDCFPO) \nvii.  National Livestock Mission (NLM)  \nviii. Livestock Health and Disease Control (LH & DC) \nix. Livestock Census (LC) and Integrated Sample Survey (ISS) \n \n\n \n(b) The details of funds allocated/ released and utilized under animal husban dry and dairying in Madhya \nPradesh during last three years and current year is as under: \n(Rs. in lakh) \n 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 (till \nOct, 2019) \nRGM Funds Released 850.00 1618.48 2852.32 2155.86 \nFunds Utilized 850.00 1618.48 989.32 0.00 \nNPDD Funds Released 155.21 358.83 2085.27 1503.33 \nFunds Utilized 155.21 358.83 1229.22 0.00 \nNDP-I Funds Released 357.00 422.00 188.00 9.00 \nFunds Utilized 387.00 180.00 367.00 58.00 \nDEDS Funds Allocated 525.00 816.43 1826.00 2939.02 \nSubsidy disbursed 494.17 819.71 1032.06 186.45 \nNLM Funds Released 1278.96 48.00 1247.04 0.00 \nFunds Utilized 1179.67 48.00 874.72 0.00 \nLH & \nDC \nFunds Released 419.25 1717.10 2944.55 180.00 \nFunds Utilized 399.00 1310.65 2842.31 0.00 \nLC & \nISS \nFunds Released 121.24 117.96 402.17* 322.22 \nFunds Utilized 85.28 100.72 236.45 141.5 \nNote: State-wise fund allocation is not done under NPDD and NDP-I. \nNDP-I phase –I is going to close in November, 2019. NDP -I scheme has been discontinued w.r.t.  release of \nfund during 2019-20. \n*The amount includes the revalidated amount of Rs. 85.57 lakhs released during the year 2014-15 \n \n(c)  For employment generation and promotion of entrepreneurship in dairy and small ruminant sector \nespecially in rural areas, the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying is implementing two schemes, \nnamely, Dairy Entrepreneurship Development Scheme , and Entrepreneurship Development and \nEmployment Generation across the country including Madhya Pradesh .  The State-wise list of number of \nentrepreneurs benefitt ed and amount of subsidy disbursed under the scheme during last three years and \ncurrent year is at Annexure. \n*** \n\nAnnexure  \nDAIRY ENTREPRENEURSHIP DEVELOPMENT SCHEME (DEDS) (TILL 31.10.2019) \n(Rs. in lakh) \nS.No \n \nState \n \n2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 \nUnits Amount Units Amount Units Amount Units Amount \n1 Andaman and Nicobar  16 2.48 23  3.50 8 2.00 0  0.00 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 4121 1582.12 11534  4575.96 2660 1810.51 509  251.76 \n3 Bihar 1326 643.94 1248  487.63 6